<title>HONG KONG: HK bourse member found innocent on bribery charge.</title>
<headline>HK bourse member found innocent on bribery charge.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A council member and former vice chairman of the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong, Chen Po-sum, was found not guilty of bribery by a High Court jury, government radio reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Chen, 66, had been charged with accepting more than HK$1.5 million in connection with the transfer of seats at the exchange.</p>
</text>
